hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27756","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Idris who said: I heard al-Amash narrate from Shaqiq from Khabbab who said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so of us are those who died and did not consume anything of their reward, of them Musab ibn Umayr; he left nothing except a namira cloak; when they covered his head with it his feet showed, and when we covered his feet his head showed; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Cover his head and put idhkhir upon his feet; he said: And of us are those whose fruits ripened and he is plucking them."
"27757","Haddathana Abu Muawiya who said: Haddathana al-Amash from Umara ibn Umayr from Abu Mamar who said: We said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr; he said: Yes; he said: So we said: By what thing did you know that; so he said: By the movement of his beard."
"27758","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Ismail who said: Haddathana Qays who said: I came to Khabbab visiting him while he had been cauterized seven times in his belly, and I heard him say: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it."
"27759","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Ismail who said: Haddathana Qays from Khabbab who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was cushioning a burda in the shade of the Kaba, so we said: Will you not seek victory for us from Allah, mighty and majestic, or, meaning, seek victory for us; so he said: There was a man among those before you who would be taken and a pit dug for him in the earth, and a saw brought and placed upon his head and made into two halves, and that would not turn him from his religion; and he would be combed with combs of iron what is below his bone of flesh or sinew, and that would not turn him from his religion; and by Allah, Allah will complete this affair until the rider travels from Madina to Hadramawt fearing none except Allah, mighty and majestic, and the wolf over his sheep; but you are hasty."
"27760","Haddathana Rawh who said: Haddathana Abu Yunus al-Qushayri from Simak ibn Harb from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt who said: Haddathani my father Khabbab ibn al-Aratt who said: While we were sitting at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waiting for him to come out for Zuhr prayer, he came out to us and said: Listen; so we said: We have heard; then he said: Listen; so we said: We have heard; so he said: Indeed there will be rulers over you, so do not aid them in their wrongdoing nor believe them in their lies; for whoever aids them in their wrongdoing and believes them in their lies will never come to me at the Hawd."
"27761","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam who said: Haddathana Israil from Abu Ishaq from Haritha ibn Mudarrib who said: I entered upon Khabbab while he had been cauterized seven times, so he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it; and I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owning not a dirham, and indeed in the side of my house now there are forty thousand dirhams; he said: Then his shroud was brought, and when he saw it he wept and said: But Hamza, there was found for him no shroud except a striped burda; when it was placed upon his head it shrank from his feet, and when it was placed upon his feet it shrank from his head, until it was extended upon his head and idhkhir was placed upon his feet."
